<p>A request for "chickpeas" with no type is like ordering "rice" without naming a variety. It is technically an order, but it won't get you a quote you can compare. Kabuli and desi are different products commercially. They serve different end uses, grow as separate crops and are priced independently. This guide is for importers, canners, hummus and snack manufacturers, and dal processors deciding which type and grade to buy from India. It covers size grading, colour, moisture and defect tolerances, what moves the price, and the mistakes that cause disputes. For market-specific ports and paperwork, see our country guides.</p>

