<p><strong>What the trade data can and can't tell you about grade.</strong> HS 0713.20 covers kabuli and desi together, so the destination table doesn't split the two. The value per kilogram does, however, hint at the mix. From the same WITS figures, Algeria's 2024 shipments averaged more than twice the value per kilogram of Bangladesh's. Egypt, the United States, Sri Lanka and Saudi Arabia also sit well above the average. That fits large-kabuli buying in Mediterranean, Middle Eastern and North American markets and desi-heavy buying in South Asia, but it is an inference, not a labelled statistic. The trend is clearer. India's chickpea exports roughly tripled in value from 2021 to 2023. In 2024 volume fell by about 16% while value held almost flat, so the average value per kilogram rose.</p>
